Subject: [PATCH 02323/11362] [outer-loop] ARC move-distance heuristic: 8-conn
 misplaced-REGION count (the breakthrough)

Built + validated the move-distance-aware heuristic the cell-count ceiling
called for: misplaced_region_distance(win) = number of 8-connected connected
components in (grid != WIN) -- the count of distinct 'wrong regions'. It is
MOVE-ALIGNED (one action ~ fixes one region -> drops ~1/move), giving both the
right scale (~moves, not cells) AND a real gradient, which a cell-count lacks.

Validated A/B (v2-A*, budget 8000, vs pure BFS) across 8 games -- HELPS 5,
NEUTRAL 3, REGRESSES 0:
  r11l 3/257  (OPTIMAL path, -88% exp; NO cell-count weight could do both)
  sk48 14/2496 (-43%; cell-count FAILS this game entirely 0/8000)
  m0r0 15/6188 (solves where BFS exhausts 8000, at registry-optimal 15 acts)
  ls20 13/1317 (-26%) ; su15 7/1574 (-10%, but H0 better -> su15 keeps H0)
  cd82/sp80/tu93 neutral (tiny no-headroom games; no longer paths, still repro)
It cracks exactly the high-cell-impact games (r11l/m0r0/sk48) that defeated
every cell-count heuristic. (Caught + fixed a measurement bug first: heuristics
took a grid but v2 passes a frame -> threw -> v2 try/except returned constant
1e9 -> A* silently == BFS. Wrap with grid_of.)

Shipped: the reusable factory + 5 asserting unit tests (zero-at-win, region-
counting, 8-vs-4-conn, finite-float, monotone-under-fix); reproduction-gated
CAPTURES to gap_fills/ for r11l/ls20/m0r0/sk48 (self-contained, re-verified via
the full load path, bundle-able offline); gap_fill prompt now steers the LLM to
the proven region-count form (ndi in exec scope + bundle). gap_fills now:
ls20,m0r0,r11l,sk48,su15. Principle: verify goal STRUCTURE (distinct things
wrong), not SURFACE (pixels differing) -- same lens as the energy verifier.
